WEBVTT

00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:05.620
<i>Monsters threaten human life.</i>

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:09.660
<i>They are opposed by brave adventurers!</i>

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:14.550
And I, Alvin, am one of them!

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:18.500
Now in a party with Carla, the healer,

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:21.360
my journey continues!

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:43.350
Don't Hurt Me,

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:43.350
Don't Hurt Me,

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:43.350
My Healer!

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:59.760
<b>As usual, Alvin and Carla have to overcome a series of crises...</b>

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:56.920
What a nice old lady.

00:01:56.920 --> 00:01:59.750
She gave us so many medicinal 
herbs and provisions!

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:01.680
Such generosity.

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:04.650
Yeah, thanks to her, our guild 
quest is as good as complete.

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:08.060
But it was pretty dicey, at first.

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:10.030
She was so mad about all we did to her...

00:02:11.870 --> 00:02:12.910
Fire safety first!

00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:14.240
Blast!

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:19.960
Why did you have to make that 
old lady so angry, Alvin-san?

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:21.360
Honestly, a grown man...

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:23.670
You're the main one she was mad at!

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:27.420
But then your spell turned her young again,

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:29.300
and made her so happy she cried.

00:02:30.050 --> 00:02:32.720
I can't thank you enough, Carla-sama!

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:35.300
<b>Carla-sama</b>

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:35.300
She even put a damned 
"-sama" after your name.

00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:37.630
All's well that ends well, I guess.

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:41.290
Now, let's get back to the guild 
and hand over the medicinal herbs.

00:02:42.230 --> 00:02:43.620
By the way, Carla.

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:45.070
You're being awfully quiet.

00:02:45.070 --> 00:02:47.050
Isn't that a sign of the apocalypse?

00:02:47.050 --> 00:02:47.970
Hush!

00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:51.240
What's up, Big Sis Carla?

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:54.240
Oh, heck. Am I right about 
that apocalypse thing?

00:02:54.550 --> 00:02:56.230
Okay, guys, nobody move!

00:02:56.750 --> 00:03:03.110
If y-you dom wamma bie, wep astay 
lom the staggon en gibbe mer yunny!

00:03:04.730 --> 00:03:05.630
What now?

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:12.130
Let me try that again!

00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:13.880
Sure!

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:14.730
Awesome!

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:17.260
Who's that?

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:18.210
I don't know.

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:20.500
She seems to be some kind of a thief.

00:03:21.230 --> 00:03:22.390
I'm coming out!

00:03:22.390 --> 00:03:23.890
Right!

00:03:26.390 --> 00:03:28.710
Okay, guys, nobody move!

00:03:28.710 --> 00:03:32.000
If you don't wanna to die, 
step away from the wagon and—

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:36.910
It's okay!

00:03:36.910 --> 00:03:37.810
You made it! You're good!

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:43.590
Do it again! Do it again!

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:44.980
Do it again!

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:45.690
Stop it!

00:03:45.690 --> 00:03:47.970
Look, we got the point.

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:50.810
You want us to give you the wagon, right?

00:03:50.810 --> 00:03:51.490
Is that it?

00:03:51.800 --> 00:03:54.020
You mean, I don't have to do it again?

00:03:54.020 --> 00:03:55.300
Yeah, you're good!

00:03:56.190 --> 00:03:58.100
Does that mean you'll give me your wagon?

00:03:58.100 --> 00:03:59.170
No freaking way.

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:00.440
Stingy!

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:00.670
<b>Bzzt</b>

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:00.670
<b>Bzzt</b>

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:01.740
You bet I am!

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:03.320
You think life's all about handouts?

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:05.150
Anyway, are you supposed to be a thief?

00:04:05.150 --> 00:04:07.050
You do seem to be on your own...

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:08.990
I'm not alone.

00:04:08.990 --> 00:04:10.800
I'm the oldest of four sisters!

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:12.920
That's not what I meant.

00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:14.320
Okay, listen up!

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:16.570
What is it now?

00:04:16.570 --> 00:04:19.340
You're not supposed to 
just burst out and shout!

00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:22.960
Everyone knows a thief is supposed 
to lie in wait and mount an ambush!

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:27.800
And if you've got sisters, you should 
bring some of them to help out!

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:30.440
Actually, they're still too little...

00:04:30.910 --> 00:04:34.190
A monster, lecturing a human 
on how to ambush travelers...

00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:36.310
I just got a great idea!

00:04:36.310 --> 00:04:39.580
And then the holy woman 
weighs in with advice.

00:04:39.580 --> 00:04:41.670
When there are multiple 
opponents to be ambushed,

00:04:41.670 --> 00:04:43.790
you should always try to 
take one of them hostage!

00:04:43.790 --> 00:04:44.880
Oh!

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:48.220
And in honor of the occasion, 
I volunteer for the role!

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:50.470
Wow, really? That's so nice.

00:04:50.780 --> 00:04:53.980
But do you think that warrior 
is going to play along?

00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:55.290
It's okay.

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:57.730
If there's one thing he's good 
at, it's reading the mood.

00:04:58.040 --> 00:04:59.480
Okay...

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:02.890
Is this good? Not too tight?

00:05:02.890 --> 00:05:04.530
It's just fine.

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:07.240
Now, try threatening me to Alvin-san.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:09.920
Hey, hey, hey! Nobody move!

00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:12.240
Drat! When did you...

00:05:14.730 --> 00:05:18.280
If you value her life...

00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:19.920
Whisper, whisper, whisper.

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:21.870
Show me your best one-shot gag!

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:24.890
That's a hell of a hostage demand!

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:26.980
Have faith in yourself, Alvin-san!

00:05:26.980 --> 00:05:28.750
Everything you do is funny!

00:05:28.750 --> 00:05:30.370
What's that supposed to mean?!

00:05:30.750 --> 00:05:32.110
I refuse to do this!

00:05:35.240 --> 00:05:36.800
Hey... hang on, now!

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:39.350
Why are you sitting? 
I said, I'm not doing this!

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:43.700
Hey, cut it out!

00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:45.990
Don't go into spectator mode!

00:05:51.990 --> 00:05:55.530
Alvin! Alvin!

00:05:55.880 --> 00:05:57.500
Alvin!

00:05:55.880 --> 00:05:57.500
Stop pushing me!

00:05:57.500 --> 00:06:01.130
Alvin! Alvin!

00:06:01.130 --> 00:06:04.700
Alvin! Alvin!

00:06:04.700 --> 00:06:06.120
Alvin!

00:06:06.390 --> 00:06:07.760
Loser!

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:10.760
Darn it! Just close your 
eyes and wait a minute!

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:13.160
Don't open those eyes until I say so!

00:06:13.160 --> 00:06:15.150
And being a loser has 
nothing to do with this!

00:06:15.510 --> 00:06:16.760
He's doing it.

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:20.830
My best one-shot gag...

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:27.010
All right. It's ready.

00:06:28.160 --> 00:06:29.050
Now...

00:06:29.370 --> 00:06:30.390
Ta-da!

00:06:30.940 --> 00:06:33.420
I'm a dullahan!

00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:53.080
I should probably head out.

00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:54.270
Understood.

00:06:54.270 --> 00:06:55.680
Just a minute.

00:07:00.660 --> 00:07:02.360
Here, take this.

00:07:02.360 --> 00:07:03.810
Are you sure?

00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:05.960
As an apology for that terrible joke.

00:07:05.960 --> 00:07:08.430
Thanks. Goodbye.

00:07:08.950 --> 00:07:10.460
Take care!

00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:15.050
Very impressive, Alvin-san!

00:07:15.050 --> 00:07:19.360
Was that all part of your 
plan to demoralize her?

00:07:20.860 --> 00:07:22.080
Yes.

00:07:41.550 --> 00:07:43.110
Damn it...

00:07:46.470 --> 00:07:49.580
It's no use. This golem is too powerful!

00:07:49.580 --> 00:07:50.690
Alvin-san!

00:07:50.690 --> 00:07:52.100
Stand back, Carla!

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:56.120
I'll buy us time. You run—

00:07:56.120 --> 00:07:57.040
No way, no way!

00:07:57.040 --> 00:07:59.890
There's no way you are 
buying anyone any time!

00:07:59.890 --> 00:08:01.280
There's no freaking way!

00:08:01.280 --> 00:08:02.620
You sound a little too sure about that!

00:08:02.620 --> 00:08:04.260
You couldn't, even resurrected!

00:08:04.260 --> 00:08:05.580
Knock it off!

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:08.210
Will you just let me 
serve as the vanguard—

00:08:10.090 --> 00:08:12.290
Back off, buddy! We're kind of busy here!

00:08:16.950 --> 00:08:18.720
Take it easy, man.

00:08:18.990 --> 00:08:22.810
How many seconds do you expect to 
buy against a golem, Alvin-san?

00:08:22.810 --> 00:08:24.360
Not many, I'm sure.

00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:26.220
You're perpetually disadvantaged.

00:08:26.220 --> 00:08:29.470
That's a painfully convincing argument.

00:08:29.470 --> 00:08:32.230
However!

00:08:32.230 --> 00:08:35.410
You do have one unique advantage!

00:08:35.860 --> 00:08:38.550
What, my integrity?

00:08:38.550 --> 00:08:39.830
Very funny.

00:08:41.160 --> 00:08:43.320
It's me! Yay!

00:08:43.730 --> 00:08:45.170
I wish I didn't.

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:48.110
With a healer like me 
serving as your backup,

00:08:48.110 --> 00:08:50.140
this golem will fall easily!

00:08:50.410 --> 00:08:53.890
Easily? Backup?

00:08:53.890 --> 00:08:57.390
You're not going to use that deadly 
enhancement spell, are you?

00:09:00.020 --> 00:09:01.640
It'll be better this time.

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:04.230
I've matured a great deal since.

00:09:04.720 --> 00:09:05.430
Yes!

00:09:05.940 --> 00:09:07.730
You sure about that?

00:09:07.730 --> 00:09:11.040
I won't stay the same forever, 
unlike someone I know.

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:12.850
Don't point at me!

00:09:13.140 --> 00:09:14.350
Now, now.

00:09:14.350 --> 00:09:16.100
Golem-san is waiting.

00:09:16.100 --> 00:09:18.270
I promise, I'll back you up!

00:09:18.270 --> 00:09:19.870
Are you sure about this?

00:09:20.140 --> 00:09:21.490
I'll give you a nice funeral.

00:09:21.490 --> 00:09:23.310
That's <i>not</i> promising!

00:09:24.710 --> 00:09:26.880
If you insist.

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:28.330
Good luck!

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:30.080
Hey, golem!

00:09:31.580 --> 00:09:35.120
I'm a man! 
I can't spend my whole life cowering!

00:09:34.350 --> 00:09:37.800
Go! Fight! Alvin-san!

00:09:34.510 --> 00:09:42.720
<b>Fight</b>

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:42.720
<b>Alvin</b>

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:42.720
<b>Alvin-san</b>

00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:42.720
<b>Alvin</b>

00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:42.720
<b>Alvin-san</b>

00:09:35.130 --> 00:09:42.720
<b>Alvin</b>

00:09:35.130 --> 00:09:42.720
<b>Alvin-san</b>

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:42.720
<b>Go! Go!</b>

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:37.440
Let's finis—

00:09:35.260 --> 00:09:42.720
<b>Alvin</b>

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:42.720
<b>Alvin-san</b>

00:09:37.800 --> 00:09:40.980
Go, go, Alvin! Fight, fight, Alvin!

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:42.730
Let's go, Alvin!

00:09:42.730 --> 00:09:46.590
Fight an unwinnable battle 
and learn the pecking order!

00:09:46.590 --> 00:09:47.940
Oh, shut up!

00:09:47.940 --> 00:09:48.930
Hey!

00:09:48.930 --> 00:09:52.550
Well? What do you think of my new 
spell, "Cheerful Encouragement"?

00:09:52.550 --> 00:09:54.220
That sounded like heckling!

00:09:54.220 --> 00:09:56.140
It filled you with determination, didn't it?

00:09:56.140 --> 00:09:58.060
It filled me with <i>anger</i>!

00:09:58.060 --> 00:09:59.880
Aren't you supposed to do something like...

00:09:59.880 --> 00:10:01.590
raise my attack power,

00:10:01.590 --> 00:10:03.170
raise my defense power,

00:10:03.170 --> 00:10:05.040
or something that's actually useful?

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:06.420
I see!

00:10:06.420 --> 00:10:09.330
Then, I'll go into town and buy you 
an expensive sword and shield!

00:10:09.330 --> 00:10:10.370
Just a minute!

00:10:10.370 --> 00:10:11.070
Not like that, damn it!

00:10:11.070 --> 00:10:13.590
Damn it! That's all wrong!

00:10:13.850 --> 00:10:16.090
Oh, silly me!

00:10:16.090 --> 00:10:18.770
You have to give me money first.

00:10:18.770 --> 00:10:19.810
Tee-hee.

00:10:19.810 --> 00:10:21.090
It's not that!

00:10:21.090 --> 00:10:23.850
As a healer, you're supposed 
to support me with <i>spells</i>!

00:10:23.850 --> 00:10:25.600
Actually...

00:10:25.880 --> 00:10:28.570
I don't think there's an enhancement spell 
powerful enough

00:10:28.570 --> 00:10:30.140
to let you beat a golem, Alvin-san.

00:10:30.140 --> 00:10:31.740
I don't even know what to say.

00:10:30.520 --> 00:10:31.740
Is that so?

00:10:32.600 --> 00:10:37.640
After all that talk about how easy you'd 
make it, suddenly it's impossible?

00:10:39.740 --> 00:10:41.340
We have a trump card.

00:10:41.340 --> 00:10:42.360
What is it now?

00:10:42.360 --> 00:10:44.810
I do think it would give 
us the victory, but...

00:10:48.810 --> 00:10:50.870
I don't know what you're so hesitant about,

00:10:50.010 --> 00:10:50.870
Upsy-daisy!

00:10:50.870 --> 00:10:52.900
but after all this, I'll do whatever it is!

00:10:52.900 --> 00:10:55.890
We need to work together 
to defeat that golem!

00:10:56.830 --> 00:10:58.110
Alvin-san...

00:10:58.690 --> 00:10:59.890
Very well.

00:11:00.440 --> 00:11:01.880
What is it?

00:11:02.170 --> 00:11:05.030
We'll borrow power from 
the spirits of earth!

00:11:06.060 --> 00:11:07.890
That sounds really cool!

00:11:10.030 --> 00:11:13.560
It's important to pray to them very hard.

00:11:13.560 --> 00:11:16.720
Therefore, Alvin-san, 
I need you to pray with me.

00:11:16.720 --> 00:11:19.150
All right. I just have to pray, right?

00:11:19.450 --> 00:11:21.540
Now, place your hands on the ground below,

00:11:21.540 --> 00:11:23.290
and rest your head on the rocks.

00:11:26.290 --> 00:11:28.350
I'm sorry for the long wait.

00:11:28.670 --> 00:11:30.170
I...

00:11:30.170 --> 00:11:34.070
There's a favor I need to 
ask you before we fight.

00:11:34.070 --> 00:11:37.560
Is there any way you could be convinced 
to let our warrior here win?

00:11:37.860 --> 00:11:39.170
We're begging you!

00:11:39.170 --> 00:11:41.480
She tricked me!

00:11:50.790 --> 00:11:52.420
We're almost to town.

00:11:53.240 --> 00:11:56.320
I feel like something's been 
missing for a while now.

00:11:56.320 --> 00:11:58.690
He's probably off chasing butterflies again.

00:12:02.620 --> 00:12:03.450
Huh?

00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:05.200
It's the golem again!

00:12:10.670 --> 00:12:11.660
What is it?

00:12:11.660 --> 00:12:13.550
Is he trying to tell us something?

00:12:14.130 --> 00:12:16.960
Wh-What did you say?!

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:19.180
Hey, you can understand him?

00:12:19.180 --> 00:12:21.270
So? What did he say?

00:12:23.350 --> 00:12:25.460
You <i>can't</i> understand him?!

00:12:25.720 --> 00:12:29.350
Of course I can't understand him! 
That's why I asked what he said!

00:12:29.350 --> 00:12:31.490
That's what you say when 
you <i>can</i> understand him!

00:12:31.490 --> 00:12:32.500
You suck at this!

00:12:32.500 --> 00:12:34.840
Get off each other's backs 
and listen to me, guys!

00:12:34.840 --> 00:12:36.980
Hang on! So you <i>can</i> talk!

00:12:37.620 --> 00:12:40.080
I'm told that the longest-lived creatures

00:12:40.080 --> 00:12:43.450
have high intelligence and 
a wealth of experience.

00:12:43.450 --> 00:12:45.480
Not that line again.

00:12:45.480 --> 00:12:47.190
Just follow me!

00:12:47.190 --> 00:12:49.560
There's no time to lose!

00:13:03.880 --> 00:13:06.510
So, what happened to him?

00:13:06.930 --> 00:13:09.260
He appears to be poisoned.

00:13:09.260 --> 00:13:11.820
I think he was bitten by a venomous snake.

00:13:11.820 --> 00:13:15.780
Shouldn't a mushroom monster have 
a degree of toxin resistance?

00:13:15.780 --> 00:13:23.290
Unfortunately, I... I'm an 
edible species... of mushroom.

00:13:23.290 --> 00:13:25.140
I... see.

00:13:25.140 --> 00:13:26.640
Are you all right?

00:13:26.640 --> 00:13:29.270
Do you have any last words?

00:13:29.270 --> 00:13:31.960
Actually... couldn't you cast... 
an antidote spe—

00:13:31.960 --> 00:13:33.170
Don't speak!

00:13:33.170 --> 00:13:35.160
You'll make the poison spread faster!

00:13:35.160 --> 00:13:38.660
Please, don't say it's the end! 
It's too tragic to conceive!

00:13:38.660 --> 00:13:40.250
He wasn't, though!

00:13:40.520 --> 00:13:44.070
Sob, sob. I'm sure... sob, sob...

00:13:44.070 --> 00:13:46.260
we'll meet again... sob, sob, sob...

00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:49.010
in the next world... sob, sob, sob...

00:13:49.010 --> 00:13:50.980
Don't just give up!

00:13:50.980 --> 00:13:53.770
I don't think I've ever heard a person 
say "sob, sob, sob" out loud before.

00:13:53.770 --> 00:13:57.950
This is normally the part where someone 
would say such things and give up.

00:13:57.950 --> 00:14:01.010
Fortunately, you happen to be with me!

00:14:02.210 --> 00:14:05.610
Are you seeing that expression 
of total despair?

00:14:05.850 --> 00:14:07.450
Allow me to show you...

00:14:07.450 --> 00:14:10.150
the holy power of a curative specialist!

00:14:10.150 --> 00:14:12.470
Did you say specialist, or blacklist?

00:14:12.470 --> 00:14:15.610
Have you forgotten how I turned 
that old lady young again?

00:14:15.610 --> 00:14:18.670
I also remember your deadly 
enhancement spell!

00:14:18.670 --> 00:14:20.300
Are you ready?!

00:14:20.880 --> 00:14:22.860
I'm resigned to my fate.

00:14:23.700 --> 00:14:25.630
He's prepared to die!

00:14:27.220 --> 00:14:29.940
Come, rest back on this rock.

00:14:31.700 --> 00:14:33.600
Now, we'll take it slow.

00:14:35.070 --> 00:14:36.950
In a moment like this...

00:14:37.260 --> 00:14:40.320
It's going to be okay. Try to relax.

00:14:40.320 --> 00:14:41.900
Thanks...

00:14:42.510 --> 00:14:44.980
She almost looks a little 
bit like a healer...

00:14:44.980 --> 00:14:47.810
I'll put you out of your misery very soon.

00:14:48.070 --> 00:14:51.310
Never mind. Her word choice 
is still pure malevolence!

00:14:51.580 --> 00:14:54.320
Now, with this sacred left hand...

00:15:10.590 --> 00:15:12.080
What are you doing?!

00:15:12.300 --> 00:15:13.000
You...

00:15:13.000 --> 00:15:14.940
Why did you stick your hand into his mouth!

00:15:14.940 --> 00:15:16.060
Cut it out!

00:15:16.060 --> 00:15:18.300
Why? This is the antidote spell.

00:15:18.300 --> 00:15:19.610
It's torture!

00:15:19.610 --> 00:15:22.640
It's okay. I'm just trying to 
get him to expel the toxin.

00:15:22.640 --> 00:15:24.450
I hope he doesn't expel any organs!

00:15:25.170 --> 00:15:25.850
There!

00:15:28.030 --> 00:15:31.760
I did it! I got him to expel the poison!

00:15:32.980 --> 00:15:35.170
Well? How are you feeling?

00:15:35.550 --> 00:15:38.870
I'm feeling... much better...

00:15:39.280 --> 00:15:42.510
That's a healer! 
I thought I was dead for a minute there!

00:15:42.510 --> 00:15:45.690
Oh... no need to flatter me.

00:15:45.690 --> 00:15:48.570
Calling me a "goddess of healing" 
is surely too far.

00:15:48.570 --> 00:15:49.510
You're making me blush!

00:15:50.760 --> 00:15:53.520
Well? Did you see that, Alvin-san?

00:15:53.520 --> 00:15:55.260
I looked magnificently like a healer back—

00:15:59.390 --> 00:16:01.530
Medic!

00:16:04.660 --> 00:16:05.900
It's starting to come down.

00:16:06.220 --> 00:16:08.910
There's a cabin nearby. Let's get him there.

00:16:09.560 --> 00:16:10.510
Right.

00:16:18.440 --> 00:16:20.610
Thanks for all the help, Golem.

00:16:20.870 --> 00:16:23.610
We couldn't have gotten 
Alvin here without you.

00:16:24.410 --> 00:16:27.040
If we'd left it all up to Big Sis Carla,

00:16:27.040 --> 00:16:30.330
it would've taken us forever.

00:16:30.790 --> 00:16:32.640
I can't thank you enough!

00:16:32.640 --> 00:16:34.130
Hey, no problem.

00:16:34.130 --> 00:16:36.380
I'm sure you'd do the same for me.

00:16:36.380 --> 00:16:39.150
But I can't go in the cabin, 
so I should really be going.

00:16:39.150 --> 00:16:40.280
Right.

00:16:40.280 --> 00:16:42.140
I'll come by to thank you pretty soon.

00:16:42.140 --> 00:16:43.760
Sure. See you.

00:16:43.760 --> 00:16:45.140
See ya!

00:16:47.760 --> 00:16:50.390
Okay, I'd better get the antidote herbs.

00:16:50.880 --> 00:16:52.340
Stare.

00:16:52.700 --> 00:16:54.080
B-Big Sis?!

00:16:54.080 --> 00:16:56.050
How friendly you two are.

00:16:56.050 --> 00:16:57.510
I g-guess so...

00:16:57.510 --> 00:17:00.010
Go fetch the wagon, won't you?

00:17:00.010 --> 00:17:01.140
S-Sure...

00:17:01.140 --> 00:17:02.780
And give me my bag.

00:17:04.330 --> 00:17:05.450
Bag?

00:17:08.050 --> 00:17:08.820
What the...

00:17:08.820 --> 00:17:10.250
What happened to me?

00:17:10.250 --> 00:17:13.430
Right, the mushroom spat 
out the poison and—

00:17:19.600 --> 00:17:21.430
Where am I?

00:17:23.570 --> 00:17:25.950
It looks abandoned... but, a cabin?

00:17:26.530 --> 00:17:28.520
You're awake, are you?

00:17:29.310 --> 00:17:30.940
Is that you, Carla?

00:17:31.260 --> 00:17:34.500
It appears my prayers to God were answered!

00:17:34.940 --> 00:17:36.200
Evil cultist!

00:17:36.970 --> 00:17:39.340
Sorry, it was actually an angel.

00:17:39.340 --> 00:17:40.160
Isn't that nice?

00:17:40.160 --> 00:17:42.660
I'm sticking with "evil cultist"!

00:17:42.660 --> 00:17:45.830
And what's with that new outfit?

00:17:45.830 --> 00:17:47.180
Does it suit me?

00:17:47.180 --> 00:17:49.470
It does. As an evil cultist.

00:17:49.860 --> 00:17:55.600
These are my ritual robes, worn to 
ask God to make you feel better!

00:17:55.940 --> 00:17:57.060
Yay!

00:17:57.060 --> 00:18:00.380
You look more like you're 
prepared to sacrifice me!

00:18:00.380 --> 00:18:01.430
What's with the mask?!

00:18:02.310 --> 00:18:03.560
What a rude thing to say!

00:18:03.560 --> 00:18:04.350
But seriously...

00:18:04.730 --> 00:18:09.090
God would be offended by 
a sacrifice like that.

00:18:09.090 --> 00:18:10.860
I'd need something nicer, 
like a chicken, or a goat!

00:18:10.860 --> 00:18:13.180
Now I'm offended, I think.

00:18:13.180 --> 00:18:15.130
I sit, sensitively.

00:18:15.130 --> 00:18:15.890
What in the world?

00:18:15.890 --> 00:18:17.790
But how are you feeling?

00:18:18.180 --> 00:18:19.920
A lot better.

00:18:19.920 --> 00:18:23.200
You didn't stick your hand 
in my mouth, did you?

00:18:23.200 --> 00:18:26.680
Actually, I was running low on power, 
so I couldn't use that spell.

00:18:26.680 --> 00:18:27.960
I'm very sowwy.

00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:29.460
I'm <i>glad</i>.

00:18:29.750 --> 00:18:32.030
So, how did you remove the poison?

00:18:32.410 --> 00:18:34.300
With my prayers, as I said!

00:18:36.290 --> 00:18:39.570
I guess it must not have 
been very potent poison.

00:18:41.070 --> 00:18:43.610
Your face does still look a little bad.

00:18:43.610 --> 00:18:45.260
I think you mean my <i>complexion</i>.

00:18:45.260 --> 00:18:46.670
Is that how it goes?

00:18:46.670 --> 00:18:48.150
Yes! It is!

00:18:49.490 --> 00:18:51.430
Hold out your forehead!

00:18:51.430 --> 00:18:53.180
Stop that! I'm fine!

00:18:54.740 --> 00:18:58.160
I've never had my temperature 
checked with an iron claw before.

00:18:58.160 --> 00:19:01.110
You do still appear to 
have a bit of body heat.

00:19:01.110 --> 00:19:03.040
I'd be dead if I didn't!

00:19:03.390 --> 00:19:05.800
You should probably lie down.

00:19:05.800 --> 00:19:07.540
Let's cool you off.

00:19:13.040 --> 00:19:14.290
There!

00:19:14.290 --> 00:19:15.410
Wring it first!

00:19:15.410 --> 00:19:16.930
S-Sorry!

00:19:19.050 --> 00:19:20.810
Not on my <i>head</i>!

00:19:21.120 --> 00:19:23.320
Look at you, dripping with charm!

00:19:23.620 --> 00:19:26.370
Now's no time for flattery!

00:19:26.370 --> 00:19:28.120
Forgot it! Just leave me alone!

00:19:28.120 --> 00:19:29.780
Wait a minute!

00:19:29.780 --> 00:19:30.960
Oh, I know.

00:19:30.960 --> 00:19:33.610
Are you hungry, Alvin-san?

00:19:34.230 --> 00:19:36.850
Actually, I haven't eaten 
anything for a while.

00:19:36.850 --> 00:19:38.560
I guess I am a little hungry.

00:19:38.560 --> 00:19:40.470
I thought you'd say that.

00:19:40.470 --> 00:19:42.060
So I got a little something ready!

00:19:42.160 --> 00:19:47.580
<b>Eat delicious!
Medicinal Herbs Cooking</b>

00:19:42.330 --> 00:19:47.280
This book contains a number of 
recipes based on medicinal herbs.

00:19:47.780 --> 00:19:49.230
Well.

00:19:49.580 --> 00:19:50.840
Let me see!

00:19:51.170 --> 00:19:55.500
They're recipes that not only use 
the properties of medicinal herbs,

00:19:55.500 --> 00:19:57.600
but are also very tasty!

00:19:58.410 --> 00:20:00.480
So? What did you make?

00:20:03.690 --> 00:20:05.040
"Make"?

00:20:05.440 --> 00:20:07.700
I didn't even consider that.

00:20:08.250 --> 00:20:09.970
You need more imagination.

00:20:12.090 --> 00:20:13.680
I'm sorry.

00:20:13.680 --> 00:20:18.230
I'm scatterbrained, clumsy, 
and inconsiderate.

00:20:18.230 --> 00:20:19.720
I'm sorry.

00:20:19.720 --> 00:20:20.910
H-Hey...

00:20:20.910 --> 00:20:22.610
You don't have to be that depressed about it...

00:20:22.850 --> 00:20:26.220
I'm sorry that I'm so cute about it!

00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:29.830
Don't get optimistically depressed!

00:20:30.130 --> 00:20:31.470
Sheesh.

00:20:31.470 --> 00:20:33.060
Fine, don't do anything.

00:20:33.060 --> 00:20:34.680
Just give me some peace and quiet.

00:20:36.250 --> 00:20:37.250
S
a
d
.
.
.

00:20:36.790 --> 00:20:37.600
Okay.

00:20:37.600 --> 00:20:39.510
And...

00:20:42.690 --> 00:20:45.130
Well... you know.

00:20:45.760 --> 00:20:48.210
You've tried to do a lot for me.

00:20:48.210 --> 00:20:51.580
And I appreciate... the sentiment, at least.

00:20:52.540 --> 00:20:54.690
Just the sentiment, okay?

00:21:00.840 --> 00:21:04.680
I-It doesn't seem appropriate to 
say that while you're resting.

00:21:05.510 --> 00:21:07.080
Yeah, yeah.

00:21:07.080 --> 00:21:08.650
Good night.

00:21:09.890 --> 00:21:11.490
Good night.

00:21:28.860 --> 00:21:32.480
Big Sis Carla! I brought the antidote herbs.

00:21:32.480 --> 00:21:35.600
We can use these to get Alvin feeling—

00:21:40.140 --> 00:21:41.610
Oh, shucks.

00:21:41.610 --> 00:21:43.590
Looks like he's doing just fine.

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:25.390 --> 00:23:27.210
Next episode's title is...

00:23:27.210 --> 00:23:29.960
Can't we just stop abusing 
ourselves on this?

00:23:30.320 --> 00:23:32.470
Yeah, it's not possible to 
do it in fifteen seconds.

00:23:32.750 --> 00:23:33.840
It seems pretty stupid.

00:23:33.840 --> 00:23:34.940
Agreed.

00:23:34.940 --> 00:23:36.440
Oh, it's from the higher-ups.

00:23:37.010 --> 00:23:39.970
<b>See you then!</b>

00:23:37.010 --> 00:23:40.090
<b>"This show is fairly unique in that Carla is the only recurring female
character although in episode 5 we did get the witch and then the
thief character but the witch only gets a few seconds at the
end in her young form and the thief girl doesn't get any more
screen time after this so I suspect the folks at home are wondering
if we're ever going to see any new female characters and so partly
for you people this episode features a female character called
Maria Deathflame but to set up for that we have to do a zombie
story so I hope you'll enjoy that first and of course Maria has her
own idiosyncrasies so you'll just have to wait to see if it meets
your expectations and that's the deal with episode 7."</b>

00:23:37.560 --> 00:23:40.040
"We're never letting you 
people do the preview—"
